  "description": "Accessibility scanner for running Android and iOS apps, tried on native Android (Views, Jetpack Compose), native iOS (UIKit, SwiftUI) and .NET MAUI apps, with extra help for .NET MAUI. Wraps Apple's accessibility audit and Google's Accessibility Test Framework, can capture what TalkBack says on Android, maps findings to WCAG 2.2 and labels the standards they are relevant to (Section 508, EN 301 549 and others), can point findings at a likely line in your own project (--source), and writes JSON, HTML, Markdown ticket, CSV, PDF and per-criterion evidence report output. It can also share a saved run as one file, signed by default. Automated checks find only some issues; manual testing is still required.",
